NAME

ulibLoadMessage - Loads a message header/message text from disk


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibLoadMessage(struct LoadMessageCommand *MsgCmd)
                                     a0


DESCRIPTION

This function accesses the message files and retrieves a message header and
possibly message text also.

The following fields of <MsgCmd> are used:

   <Section>
        The number of the section the message is in.

   <Number>
        The number of the message to load.

   <Where>
        A pointer to a (struct Msg) where the message header will be stored.
        If this is NULL, then the message header will not be stored anywhere.

   <Flags>
        LoadText - If set, the message text will be read from disk and stored
                   in a block of memory allocated by this function with the
                   AllocMem() function.  The pointer to this memory block is
                   stored in <MessageText>.

                   To free this memory when done, you should use the following
                   command:

                   /* The +1 is for the null terminator */
                   FreeMem(MsgCmd.MessageText,
                        ulibGetMsgData(Msg, XMD_LENGTH, NULL) + 1);


        NoSoft   - If set, this will cause all soft return pairs (0x8D 0x8D)
                   in the message to be turned into spaces.

        NoFido   - If set, all FidoNet technology lines (beginning with ^A)
                   will be removed.  Unless you are writing a FidoNet-related
                   program, you should set this flag.


RETURNS

0 - Failure
1 - Success


